  "body": "Build the native `egui_dock` AI chat panel and connect it to CamCraft's live MCP loop.\n\n## Scope\n- Add a native `Tab::AiChat` pane in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`. Design an original CamCraft layout; per `crates/ui/AGENTS.md`, do not reuse SolidCraft's visual look or theme (`LICENSE-BRAND`) without written permission.\n- Run the provider turn loop on a background `std::thread` under `#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]`.\n- Poll worker events via `std::sync::mpsc` inside `state.drain_actions()` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) and wake the `ControlFlow::Wait` event loop via `EventLoopProxy::send_event(())` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_window.rs`).\n- Dispatch panel tool calls through an in-process `Inbox::channel()` (`crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs`) into `mcp_host::pump(state)` (`crates/ui/src/mcp_host.rs`).\n- Include UI controls for provider/model selection, offline-only toggle, opt-in screenshot and selection attachments, Cancel (`Arc<AtomicBool>`), per-tool-call cards, per-turn change summary, Undo Turn button, fallback Q&A warning banner, and inline Allow/Deny confirmation prompts.\n\nDone means: `egui_kittest::Harness` tests against a scripted fake transport verify chat submission, tool cards, Cancel, `post` confirmation Allow/Deny, Undo Turn, and offline mode without network access.\n\nPart of #1773\n",
